  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Adjectives before the name",
   "texto": [
    "Korean adjectives carry a special form before the name: **-(으)ㄴ**. Con raíz acabada en vocal suele añadirse **-ㄴ**; con otra consonante, **-은**: 크다 → **큰 집** (casa grande), 작다 → **작은 방** (habitación pequeña), 좋다 → **좋은 사람** (buena persona). Don't confuse this form with that of verbs in the past."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common",
   "texto": [
    "Las raíces con **ㄹ** pierden esa consonante: 길다 → **긴 머리**. The adjectives in **-하다** usually form **-한** (-); some adjectives in **ㅡ** contrast the vocal by adding the termination: - (-)))), (- (-), (-), (-). The form goes immediately in front of the name: **집이 커요** (the house is large), but **큰 집** (large house)."
   ]
  },
